🔐 Security-Hardened Guide for WSGI & ASGI Servers
🚫 Important Warning

Never run in debug mode in production.

Never use --reload in production.
These options are only for local development, as they expose stack traces, restart workers on file changes, and open up unnecessary attack surfaces.


1️⃣ Gunicorn (WSGI)
✅ Hardened Command
gunicorn myapp:wsgi_app \
  --workers 4 \
  --worker-class sync \
  --bind unix:/tmp/gunicorn.sock \
  --user nobody \
  --group nogroup \
  --access-logfile /var/log/gunicorn/access.log \
  --error-logfile /var/log/gunicorn/error.log \
  --capture-output \
  --limit-request-line 8190 \
  --limit-request-field_size 8190 \
  --timeout 30

  Explanation of Key Flags

--workers 4 → Run multiple worker processes (tune per CPU).

--bind unix:/tmp/gunicorn.sock → Use Unix socket (safer than TCP).

--user nobody --group nogroup → Drop privileges after binding.

--access-logfile / --error-logfile → Separate structured logs.

--limit-request-line & --limit-request-field_size → Mitigate request smuggling.

--timeout 30 → Kill stuck workers.

⚠️ Do not use --reload in production.



